Ptolemy's theorem: For a cyclic quadrilateral (that is, a quadrilateral inscribed in a circle), the product of the diagonals equals the sum of the products of the opposite sides. AC BD = AB CD + AD BC.
Reference: https://www2.clarku.edu/faculty/djoyce/trig/ptolemy.html#:~:text=Ptolemy's%20theorem%3A%20For%20a%20cyclic,products%20of%20the%20opposite%20sides.&text=AC%20BD%20%3D%20AB%20CD%20%2B%20AD%20BC.
